    {"id": 10, "type": "MarkdownNote", "title": "Setup and model downloads", "pos": [40, 1160], "size": [900, 560], "flags": {}, "order": 10, "mode": 0, "inputs": [], "outputs": [], "properties": {"Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"}, "widgets_values": ["## LTX 2.5 Motion Track — quality\n\n1. Install WeeTodd Nodes and restart ComfyUI.\n2. Place the LTX 2.5 Q8 paged transformer and text encoder under `ComfyUI/models/diffusion_models/` and `ComfyUI/models/text_encoders/`.\n3. Download the Motion Track IC-LoRA to `ComfyUI/models/loras/`.\n4. Load an opening image. Image fields are intentionally empty in the shared workflow.\n5. Enter one or more normalized spline paths in **Motion Track Guide (MLX)**. Each inner list controls one subject or region.\n6. Confirm the colored guide in **Preview Image**. The current point is blue and its older trail ages through cyan, green, yellow, and red.\n7. Describe the visible action and sound, then queue the workflow after **LTX 2.5 Preflight** succeeds.\n\nThis workflow uses full CFG++ quality: eight sampling steps and 15 real transformer forwards. Motion Track requires its dedicated adapter; do not substitute Union Control or feed an ordinary source movie directly.\n\n### Downloads\n\n- [LTX 2.5 model components](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.5)\n- [LTX 2.3 Motion Track IC-LoRA](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.3-22b-IC-LoRA-Motion-Track-Control)\n\nQueue the workflow only after all selected files resolve under `ComfyUI/models/` or a shared model root."]}
